{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system","id":1004477,"title":"Everybody's rebel, go against the system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T09:37:21-08:00","id":1004477,"title":"Everybody's rebel, go against the system","content":"I'm just curious, what would be your idea about a rebel in different splats. Like, what character would you imagine when you consider different splats and their organisations and one (or several) character that goes straight against, but still holds onto some &quot;morals&quot;, i.e. still mage, but not a banisher. The idea is freedom loving character, who does what he wants, maybe a loner. Total fluff question here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12666-thestyx","name":"TheStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12666_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:17:27-08:00","id":1004506,"title":"","content":"The various non-committed splats. Ghost Wolves, Unaligned, Apostates, Uncalled, etc, etc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:34:54-08:00","id":1004513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system?p=1004506#post1004506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The various non-committed splats. Ghost Wolves, Unaligned, Apostates, Uncalled, etc, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, the various non-traditional splats. Iron Masters, Carthians, Free Council, etc. The former are more separate from their supernatural society as a whole, while the latter have assimilated into their supernatural culture but stand opposed to some of its more traditional elements. Either works as an archetypal &quot;rebel&quot;, it's just a matter of what they rebel against and to what degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:46:53-08:00","id":1004524,"title":"","content":"Furthermore with werewolf you have the Pure, who go against Luna in favor of Father Wolf. And various lodges that serve non-Urfarah related spirits.<br /> <br /> Mages you have Scelesti, who embrace the Abyss rather than the Supernal. Banishers who view magic as something abhorrent. Seers who serve the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> It's all there already for the most part. Even Changeling has privateers and loyalists. I'd go so far as to argue it is the 'standard' way of developing antagonists for the gamelines during their development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T00:29:04-08:00","id":1008447,"title":"","content":"One mans &quot;Freedom Fighter&quot; (Rebel) is another mans &quot;Terrorist&quot;. Though, loyalists, and integrators, seem more like the opposite of rebel to me, they work for the man. Where in that case the main splat (Changeling/Demon) by definition is actually a &quot;rebel&quot; of sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:15:51-08:00","id":1008709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system?p=1004524#post1004524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore with werewolf you have the Pure, who go against Luna in favor of Father Wolf. And various lodges that serve non-Urfarah related spirits.<br /> <br /> Mages you have Scelesti, who embrace the Abyss rather than the Supernal. Banishers who view magic as something abhorrent. Seers who serve the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those examples gave in to their respective Men.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:11:40-08:00","id":1008998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system?p=1008709#post1008709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of those examples gave in to their respective Men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly.<br /> <br /> To the Pure, Moon is 'The Man.' Complete with silver brands to mark you as his property and a list of rules he demands you follow. To the Bale Hounds and Ghost Wolves, sometimes the whole Forsaken and Pure scuffle is. Why devote yourself to some mindless internecine violence when you can do what you want and have fun?<br /> <br /> To mages, the Abyss is as far from 'The Man' as you can go. It's the forbidden, the ultimate outlaw act and then only due to a rivalry formed thousands of years ago and perpetuated by the greatest tyrannies in mage society, the Seers and the Pentacle. Banishers see Magic itself as 'The Man.' And while some Seers may see themselves as giving into 'The Man,' they appreciate that it's a better option than struggling for no reason against the laws of the world and its creators. Plus they're still in the minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-27-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T17:04:15-08:00","id":1009089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system?p=1008998#post1008998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the Pure, Moon is 'The Man.' Complete with silver brands to mark you as his property and a list of rules he demands you follow. To the Bale Hounds and Ghost Wolves, sometimes the whole Forsaken and Pure scuffle is. Why devote yourself to some mindless internecine violence when you can do what you want and have fun?<br /> <br /> To mages, the Abyss is as far from 'The Man' as you can go. It's the forbidden, the ultimate outlaw act and then only due to a rivalry formed thousands of years ago and perpetuated by the greatest tyrannies in mage society, the Seers and the Pentacle. Banishers see Magic itself as 'The Man.' And while some Seers may see themselves as giving into 'The Man,' they appreciate that it's a better option than struggling for no reason against the laws of the world and its creators. Plus they're still in the minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rhetoric aside, Pure are literally slaves to their totems. Lunes leave forsaken to their own devices unless they want specific recognition for their deeds, while abyssal entities and exarchic ministers literally take your soul with their bargains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:40:14-08:00","id":1009146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1004477-everybody-s-rebel-go-against-the-system?p=1009089#post1009089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rhetoric aside, Pure are literally slaves to their totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just said 'Rhetoric aside.' Pure are not 'literally slaves to their totems.' They tend to pick powerful totems that have harsh bans. This is not 'literally slavery.' It was more harsh in first edition because the bans could require Harmony-reducing acts that led inevitably to becoming zi'ir, but bans are not solely a Pure concept. Aside from that, what does it have to do with anything? They're rebelling against the established authority of Luna and her Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunes leave forsaken to their own devices unless they want specific recognition for their deeds </div> </div> </div>Lunes are just as capable of being tyrants as any other spirit. Luna has a mandate she's extended not just to werewolves but to all of humanity and the Hisil. Cross the line, her werewolves will get you. She's the ultimate authoritarian in werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> while abyssal entities and exarchic ministers literally take your soul with their bargains. </div> </div> </div>Some might. It doesn't really have a bearing on whether they're rebels or not, though. The Exarchs and Seers are certainly as close to the 'establishment' as you can get, but just being one is rebelling against the domineering practices of the Pentacle. Cipher and his steak versus the militaristic Zion warriors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-27-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":